OHOS: implement that C ABI by reusing the existing OCR engine code, since
the HAP cannot exec the upstream out-of-process OCR worker. Keeps the
thread-safe engine handle, size/pixel-count validation, and paired
alloc/free discipline from the out-of-process implementation, and reuses the
existing JSON result protocol rather than inventing a second one across the
FFI boundary; includes the existing boundary unit tests.

Drops a Config struct, a TextDetectionProcessing::recognition_width method
and a worker_event structured-log helper that this in-process bridge copied
in while adapting from the out-of-process worker: none of the three are ever
constructed or called anywhere in this file (resize/processing policy is
passed straight to make_engine_for_models instead), so they were dead code
rather than behavior this bridge depends on.

